---
components: ["ComparisonBar"]
description: Comparison bar sets a value against a previous one as two thin bars, with an optional relative change.
---

<script>
  import { Stack } from "carbon-components-svelte";
  import { ComparisonBar } from "carbon-components-svelte/viz";
</script>

`ComparisonBar` is part of the data visualization subpackage. Import it from `carbon-components-svelte/viz` and load `carbon-components-svelte/css/viz.css` alongside `all.css`. With a single-theme stylesheet such as `g100.css`, load the matching `viz-g100.css` instead. The subpackage is experimental: its API may change in a minor release.

## Basic

Pass `value`, `previous`, and a `label`. Both bars are scaled against the larger of the two. The comparison bar is always neutral.

<ComparisonBar value={1284} previous={912} label="Orders this period against the previous one" />

## Row labels

<ComparisonBar
  value={1284}
  previous={912}
  valueLabel="This week"
  previousLabel="Last week"
  label="Orders"
/>

## Delta

Set `showDelta` to write the relative change with a [DeltaIndicator](/components/DeltaIndicator). Set `positive` to `"down"` for metrics where lower is better.

<Stack gap={6}>
  <ComparisonBar value={1284} previous={912} showDelta label="Orders" />
  <ComparisonBar
    value={182}
    previous={240}
    positive="down"
    showDelta
    format={(value) => `${value} ms`}
    label="Median latency"
  />
</Stack>

## Format

`format` takes `Intl.NumberFormat` options or a function.

<ComparisonBar
  value={128400}
  previous={91200}
  format={{ style: "currency", currency: "USD", notation: "compact" }}
  showDelta
  label="Revenue"
/>

## Color

Set `color` to a semantic name, a categorical index from 1 to 14, a viz token name, or any CSS color.

<ComparisonBar value={1284} previous={912} color={3} label="Orders" />

## Sizes

<Stack gap={6}>
  <ComparisonBar value={1284} previous={912} showDelta size="sm" label="Small" />
  <ComparisonBar value={1284} previous={912} showDelta label="Medium (default)" />
  <ComparisonBar value={1284} previous={912} showDelta size="lg" label="Large" />
</Stack>

## Missing baseline

Without a `previous` value, the comparison row and the delta show a dash.

<ComparisonBar value={1284} previous={null} showDelta label="Orders, first period" />

## Accessibility

The bars are a two row table: the `label` is its caption and each row label is a row header. Set `headerLabels` to translate the visually hidden column headers. The bars are hidden from assistive technology because the value column carries the same information. The delta announces its direction in words. Without a `label`, the whole graphic is hidden.
